Specification CommonMark

DataType Markdown
Description Markdown source text.
Examples: ValidValues
| Value           | IsValid | Notes |
| """Hello"""     | True    |       |
| """# Heading""" | True    |       |

DataType Html
Description HTML produced from Markdown.
Examples: ValidValues
| Value                  | IsValid | Notes |
| """<p>Hello</p>"""     | True    |       |
| """<h1>Heading</h1>""" | True    |       |

Attributes MarkdownRendering
| Name     | DataType |
| Markdown | Markdown |
| Html     | Html     |
| Notes    | String   |

ScenarioGroup Paragraphs

Scenario Render Plain Paragraph
Description Plain text is rendered as a paragraph.
Examples: MarkdownRendering
| Markdown          | Html                     | Notes                  |
| """Hello world""" | """<p>Hello world</p>""" | Single-line paragraph. |
| """CommonMark"""  | """<p>CommonMark</p>"""  | Simple text.           |

ScenarioGroup Headings

Scenario Render ATX Headings
Description Hash characters create headings.
Examples: MarkdownRendering
| Markdown          | Html                   | Notes            |
| """# Heading"""   | """<h1>Heading</h1>""" | Level 1 heading. |
| """## Heading"""  | """<h2>Heading</h2>""" | Level 2 heading. |
| """### Heading""" | """<h3>Heading</h3>""" | Level 3 heading. |

ScenarioGroup Emphasis

Scenario Render Emphasis
Description Asterisks create emphasis and strong emphasis.
Examples: MarkdownRendering
| Markdown         | Html                                        | Notes            |
| """*text*"""     | """<p><em>text</em></p>"""                  | Emphasis.        |
| """**text**"""   | """<p><strong>text</strong></p>"""          | Strong emphasis. |
| """***text***""" | """<p><em><strong>text</strong></em></p>""" | Nested emphasis. |

ScenarioGroup Links

Scenario Render Links
Description Markdown links are rendered as anchor elements.
Examples: MarkdownRendering
| Markdown                           | Html                                                 | Notes         |
| """[Home](/)"""                    | """<p><a href="/">Home</a></p>"""                    | Relative URL. |
| """[Google](https://google.com)""" | """<p><a href="https://google.com">Google</a></p>""" | Absolute URL. |

ScenarioGroup Lists

Scenario Render Unordered Lists
Description Dash-prefixed items become unordered lists.
Examples: MarkdownRendering
| Markdown | Html | Notes |
| """      |      |       |
- A
""" | """<ul><li>A</li></ul>""" | Single-item list. |
| """ |
- A
- B
""" | """<ul><li>A</li><li>B</li></ul>""" | Two-item list. |

Scenario Render Ordered Lists
Description Number-prefixed items become ordered lists.
Examples: MarkdownRendering
| Markdown | Html | Notes |
| """      |      |       |
1. A
""" | """<ol><li>A</li></ol>""" | Single-item list. |
| """ |
1. A
2. B
""" | """<ol><li>A</li><li>B</li></ol>""" | Two-item list. |

ScenarioGroup Code

Scenario Render Inline Code
Description Backticks create inline code.
Examples: MarkdownRendering
| Markdown     | Html                           | Notes        |
| """`code`""" | """<p><code>code</code></p>""" | Inline code. |

Scenario Render Fenced Code Block
Description Triple backticks create a code block.
Examples: MarkdownRendering
| Markdown | Html | Notes |
| """      |      |       |